    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35313" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-opportūnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very seasonable</i>, <i>very
				convenient</i> or <i>opportune</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diversorium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 57, 234</span></i>
			: victoria, 
			<i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				6, 6, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 10, 45, 2</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕropportūnē</span></b> , <i>very seasonably</i>, <i>very
				opportunety</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 6, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fortuna te obtulit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 5, 15, § 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc cecidit quod, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 2, 4, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum sumere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					42</span></i>
			.</div>
